Title:  A Return to These Truths

Seq:    12.6.117.1.2

Level:  6 - Subdetail

Class:  quote

Attribution: [[Obama, Barack|Barack Obama]], 2009, from the speech "[[Obama's 2009 Inaugral Address]]"

Timestamp: 20251007210243

Date Added: 2025-10-07 15:02:43 -0600

Date Modified: 2026-10-15 12:27:06 -0600

Referenced In: Values form one element of a group's culture

Body:

Our challenges may be new. The instruments with which we meet them may be new. But those values upon which our success depends -- hard work and honesty, courage and fair play, tolerance and curiosity, loyalty and patriotism -- these things are old. These things are true. They have been the quiet force of progress throughout our history. What is demanded then is a return to these truths.

